{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And let them gather all the food.</b> This is the fifth. And it says 'all the food' — that they should take it from the wheat and from the barley and the spelt and oats and rye and rice and millet and similar things." "<b>And let them store up grain.</b> It is an expression of storing beneath the ground, as it is said (Job 27:16): ״אם יצבור כעפר כסף״. He gave him counsel to hide it beneath the ground and also to store it in chambers above ground, for the expression of storing includes everything, from the language of (Exodus 8:10): ״ויצברו אותם חמרים חמרים״." "<b>Under the hand of Pharaoh.</b> Under his authority and in his storehouses. <b>Food in the cities.</b> All stored food shall be kept hidden in that city. <b>And they shall keep</b> — that is, it must be something that keeps preserved for eating over a long time."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:26.929248613Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}